<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:io="clr-namespace:Bonsai.IO;assembly=Bonsai.System"
                 xmlns:orc="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:cal="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core.Calibration;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:cv="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Vision;assembly=Bonsai.Vision"
                 xmlns:vid="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Video;assembly=OpenRigs.Video"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:vc="clr-namespace:CoenQcCalibrateValve;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:p3="clr-namespace:Harp.StepperDriver;assembly=Harp.StepperDriver"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>Delivers water on one valve at a reward's pulse width (Pip, 11 Nov 2026), so a valve's calibration can be checked by weighing what it gives: Pulses pulses of SizeMs on Channel, one every SizeMs plus InterPulseIntervalMs. rig-control's Calibrations page works out the width and the pulses from the valve's curve (1 ml at the reward size) and launches it with the board as its rig.yml gives it (PortName, OutputPulseEnable). On a rig with a lick spout stage the spouts go forward first and back after, as for a calibration (Spouts, main.bonsai's). Ready once the board answers and the spouts are in; Go fires the pulses, reporting each as the delivered metric; Finished once the last has landed. Nothing is written.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl) over TCP 5561, which the rig agent relays. Reports Recording at Go.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Recording</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="PortName" DisplayName="PortName" Description="The behavior board's serial port: rig.yml's behaviorBoard: main: portName, which rig-control gives at launch." />
        <Property Name="OutputPulseEnable" DisplayName="OutputPulseEnable" Description="The board lines that pulse, such as DO1, DO2: rig.yml's pulseController outputPulseEnable, which rig-control gives at launch." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The behavior board on PortName, with the PulseController pulsing the OutputPulseEnable lines: its TriggerCalibratedPulse fires one pulse of a given width on a line, as in a session. Ready 1 s after the board's first event, once the PulseController's setup has gone out, and once the spouts are in (SpoutsReady).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Boolean">
              <rx:Name>SpoutsReady</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="PortName" DisplayName="PortName" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.BehaviorBoard.bonsai">
              <CommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</CommandsSubjectName>
              <PortName>COMx</PortName>
              <DumpRegisters>true</DumpRegisters>
              <Heartbeat>Enabled</Heartbeat>
              <EventsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</EventsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="OutputPulseEnable" DisplayName="OutputPulseEnable" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.PulseController.bonsai">
              <BehaviorCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BehaviorCommandsSubjectName>
              <OutputPulseEnable>DO1 DO2</OutputPulseEnable>
              <PulseDO1>10</PulseDO1>
              <PulseDO2>10</PulseDO2>
              <PulseDO3>10</PulseDO3>
              <BehaviorEventsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BehaviorEventsSubjectName>
              <TriggerPulseSubjectName>TriggerPulse</TriggerPulseSubjectName>
              <TriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>TriggerCalibratedPulse</TriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Delay">
                <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SpoutsReady</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Ready</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Channel" DisplayName="Channel" Description="The valve's behavior board line, 1 to 3 (DO1 to DO3): one rig.yml lists in outputPulseEnable. rig-control gives it at launch." />
        <Property Name="SizeMs" DisplayName="SizeMs" Description="Each pulse's width in ms: the reward size's, read off the valve's curve by rig-control." />
        <Property Name="Pulses" DisplayName="Pulses" Description="How many pulses: 1 ml at the reward size, by rig-control." />
        <Property Name="InterPulseIntervalMs" DisplayName="InterPulseIntervalMs" Description="The gap after each pulse, in ms: 63, as the calibration's (config\valve-calibration.yml)." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Deliver</Name>
        <Description>At Go, Pulses pulses of SizeMs on Channel through TriggerCalibratedPulse (DeliverBurst, src\Extensions), each reported as the delivered metric (how many so far); once the last has landed, Finished, and Delivered ends, which takes the spouts back.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Channel" />
              <Property Name="SizeMs" />
              <Property Name="Pulses" />
              <Property Name="InterPulseIntervalMs" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="vc:DeliverBurst">
                <vc:Channel>1</vc:Channel>
                <vc:SizeMs>1</vc:SizeMs>
                <vc:Pulses>0</vc:Pulses>
                <vc:InterPulseIntervalMs>63</vc:InterPulseIntervalMs>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TriggerCalibratedPulse</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:ElementIndex" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>it.Index + 1</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>delivered</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Last" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Finished</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject">
              <Name>Delivered</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="StepperDriver1PortName" DisplayName="StepperDriver1PortName" Description="The lick spout stage's first StepperDriver board (motors 1 to 3), rig.yml's stepperDriver: a: portName, which rig-control gives at launch; empty on a rig with no stage, which then moves nothing." />
        <Property Name="StepperDriver2PortName" DisplayName="StepperDriver2PortName" Description="The stage's second StepperDriver board (motors 4 and 5), rig.yml's stepperDriver: b: portName, which rig-control gives at launch." />
        <Property Name="SpoutMotor1Position" DisplayName="SpoutMotor1Position" Description="The in-position of motor 1 (the base), in steps from its home switch: rig-control gives each motor's from the newest mouse's calibration\LickSpoutPositions\&lt;mouse&gt;.csv, its columns motor 1 to 5." />
        <Property Name="SpoutMotor2Position" DisplayName="SpoutMotor2Position" Description="The in-position of motor 2 (the left spout's), in steps." />
        <Property Name="SpoutMotor3Position" DisplayName="SpoutMotor3Position" Description="The in-position of motor 3 (the right spout's), in steps." />
        <Property Name="SpoutMotor4Position" DisplayName="SpoutMotor4Position" Description="The in-position of motor 4 (the left spout's), in steps." />
        <Property Name="SpoutMotor5Position" DisplayName="SpoutMotor5Position" Description="The in-position of motor 5 (the right spout's), in steps." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Spouts</Name>
        <Description>The spouts forward for the delivery, as main.bonsai's Spouts (copied 11 Nov 2026), so the drops land as in a session: on a rig with a lick spout stage (StepperDriver1PortName given), Stage zeroes it and moves it to a mouse's in-position before Ready, and takes the spouts back once the water is delivered; on one without, SpoutsReady at once. Last in the workflow, after the Deliver group whose Delivered it watches.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="StepperDriver1PortName" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value />
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="StepperDriver2PortName" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value />
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="SpoutMotor1Position" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="IntProperty">
                <Value>0</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="SpoutMotor2Position" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="IntProperty">
                <Value>0</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="SpoutMotor3Position" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="IntProperty">
                <Value>0</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="SpoutMotor4Position" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="IntProperty">
                <Value>0</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="SpoutMotor5Position" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="IntProperty">
                <Value>0</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>Stage?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>it.Item1 != ""</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>Stage</Name>
              <Description>The lick spout stage, only on a rig whose rig.yml has one. Both StepperDriver boards on their ports, set up as av-dome sets them (InitialiseStepperDriverSettings, ReadSwitchStates: copied from av-dome's StepperDriver group, 10 Nov 2026), every motor zeroed on its home switch (ZEROMotors), then moved to the in-position (SpoutMotor1Position to SpoutMotor5Position, a mouse's saved positions), and SpoutsReady once the longest move has had its time. Once the water is delivered (Delivered ends), the spouts go back 1500 steps (motors 2 to 5, av-dome's both-out) and the base (motor 1) stays: a Stop moves nothing.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>StageSettings</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="harp:HarpMessage">
                    <rx:Name>StepperDriver1Commands</rx:Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>StageSettings</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="PortName" Selector="Item1" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="p3:Device">
                      <harp:OperationMode>Active</harp:OperationMode>
                      <harp:OperationLed>On</harp:OperationLed>
                      <harp:DumpRegisters>true</harp:DumpRegisters>
                      <harp:VisualIndicators>On</harp:VisualIndicators>
                      <harp:Heartbeat>Enabled</harp:Heartbeat>
                      <harp:IgnoreErrors>false</harp:IgnoreErrors>
                      <harp:PortName>COMx</harp:PortName>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject">
                    <Name>StepperDriver1Events</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="harp:HarpMessage">
                    <rx:Name>StepperDriver2Commands</rx:Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>StageSettings</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="PortName" Selector="Item2" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="p3:Device">
                      <harp:OperationMode>Active</harp:OperationMode>
                      <harp:OperationLed>On</harp:OperationLed>
                      <harp:DumpRegisters>true</harp:DumpRegisters>
                      <harp:VisualIndicators>On</harp:VisualIndicators>
                      <harp:Heartbeat>Enabled</harp:Heartbeat>
                      <harp:IgnoreErrors>false</harp:IgnoreErrors>
                      <harp:PortName>COMx</harp:PortName>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject">
                    <Name>StepperDriver2Events</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Boolean">
                    <rx:Name>SteppersZEROed</rx:Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
                    <Name>InitialiseStepperDriverSettings</Name>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>StepperDriver1Events</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                            <rx:Count>20</rx:Count>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeLast">
                            <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Delay">
                            <rx:DueTime>PT0.1S</rx:DueTime>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Unit" />
                        <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
                          <Name>Initialize StepperDriver1</Name>
                          <Workflow>
                            <Nodes>
                              <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                                <Name>Source1</Name>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateInterlockEnabledPayload">
                                  <p3:InterlockEnabled>Open</p3:InterlockEnabled>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateEnableDriverPayload">
                                  <p3:EnableDriver>Motor0 Motor1 Motor2</p3:EnableDriver>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateMotor0MaximumRunCurrentPayload">
                                  <p3:Motor0MaximumRunCurrent>0.5</p3:Motor0MaximumRunCurrent>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateMotor1MaximumRunCurrentPayload">
                                  <p3:Motor1MaximumRunCurrent>0.5</p3:Motor1MaximumRunCurrent>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateMotor2MaximumRunCurrentPayload">
                                  <p3:Motor2MaximumRunCurrent>0.5</p3:Motor2MaximumRunCurrent>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateMotor0MicrostepResolutionPayload">
                                  <p3:Motor0MicrostepResolution>Microstep8</p3:Motor0MicrostepResolution>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateMotor1MicrostepResolutionPayload">
                                  <p3:Motor1MicrostepResolution>Microstep8</p3:Motor1MicrostepResolution>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateMotor2MicrostepResolutionPayload">
                                  <p3:Motor2MicrostepResolution>Microstep8</p3:Motor2MicrostepResolution>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateEnableEncodersPayload">
                                  <p3:EnableEncoders>Encoder0 Encoder1 Encoder2</p3:EnableEncoders>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateResetEncodersPayload">
                                  <p3:ResetEncoders>Encoder0 Encoder1 Encoder2</p3:ResetEncoders>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateEncoderModePayload">
                                  <p3:EncoderMode>Position</p3:EncoderMode>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateEncoderSamplingRatePayload">
                                  <p3:EncoderSamplingRate>Rate100Hz</p3:EncoderSamplingRate>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateAccumulatedStepsSamplingRatePayload">
                                  <p3:AccumulatedStepsSamplingRate>Rate100Hz</p3:AccumulatedStepsSamplingRate>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateEnableDigitalInputsPayload">
                                  <p3:EnableDigitalInputs>Input0 Input1 Input2</p3:EnableDigitalInputs>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateInput0OpModePayload">
                                  <p3:Input0OpMode>StopMotor0OnFalling</p3:Input0OpMode>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateInput1OpModePayload">
                                  <p3:Input1OpMode>StopMotor1OnFalling</p3:Input1OpMode>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
                                <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                                <harp:Payload xsi:type="p3:CreateInput2OpModePayload">
                                  <p3:Input2OpMode>StopMotor2OnFalling</p3:Input2OpMode>
                                </harp:Payload>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="Disable">
                                <Builder xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                                  <PropertyMappings>
                                    <Property Name="Motor0StepInterval" />
                                  </PropertyMappings>
                                </Builder>
                              </Expression>
                              <Expression xsi:type="p3:CreateMessage">
